# Line endings are normalised at the repo boundary, not left to whoever's editor touched the file
# last. Without this, a Windows checkout writes CRLF, a WSL/container checkout writes LF, and every
# file either side touches shows up as a whole-file rewrite — six files in this repo were sitting
# permanently "modified" with ~1,300 lines of phantom diff that hid the real changes among them.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain text=auto: this tree gets edited from Windows and from Linux containers,
# and forcing one ending in the working tree as well as in the repo is what stops the two disagreeing.
# Every toolchain here (node, vite, eslint, prettier) is fine with LF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated; keeping it out of diffs makes review of a dependency bump readable.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
